      "items": [
        "Ideal Ammeter has ZERO resistance (connected in series); Ideal Voltmeter has INFINITE resistance (connected in parallel).",
        "If a wire is stretched to double its length, its new resistance becomes 4 times the original resistance.",
        "Galvanometer is converted into an Ammeter by connecting a low shunt resistance in parallel, and into a Voltmeter by connecting a high resistance in series."
